// WidePepper - File I/O Example
// Demonstrates file I/O concepts
// Note: Full I/O functionality requires an interpreter/evaluator

// File I/O operations are available through the builtins package:
// - pounceFile(path, mode)  - Open a file ("r"=read, "w"=write, "a"=append)
// - lapLine(handle)         - Read one line
// - devourFile(handle)      - Read entire file
// - scratchLine(handle, s)  - Write line with newline
// - scratchString(handle, s)- Write without newline
// - nuzzleClose(handle)     - Close file handle
// - sniffFile(path)         - Check if file exists
// - swatFile(path)          - Delete file
// - pounceDirectory(path)   - List directory files

// Example structure (parser support only):
yarn greeting = "File I/O Support Added!";
meow greeting;

// For now, meow is the only output mechanism
meow "I/O functions are built-in but require interpreter implementation";
